cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Code and aggregate results for "Suppress Codes, Not Patients: What
  k^m-Anonymity Costs on Complete Diagnosis Histories"
message: >-
  If you use this software or the aggregate results it contains, please cite
  both the software and the accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Pavlo
    family-names: Zamroz
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0008-8722-5769'
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Electronic Computing Machines, Lviv Polytechnic National
      University, Lviv, Ukraine
  - given-names: Kassem
    family-names: Kallas
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7689-4125'
    affiliation: 'Inserm UMR 1101 LaTIM, Brest, France'
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/clinical-ai-privacy/suppress-codes-not-patients'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24496606
abstract: >-
  The kmrel package, the scripts that produced every number, the aggregate
  results, the figure scripts and a checker that compares the tables of the
  manuscript with the results, for a study of what k^m-anonymity costs on
  complete diagnosis histories in MIMIC-IV and eICU-CRD. Contains no
  patient-level data: both databases are distributed by PhysioNet under
  credentialed data use agreements that prohibit redistribution, and counts
  between 1 and 9 are masked in the aggregate results.
keywords:
  - data anonymization
  - k^m-anonymity
  - re-identification risk
  - privacy-utility trade-off
  - electronic health records
